; The words for the NRL rules. Cards pass on to filter except words: a word's letters go to both context machines
; (OUT at let, then the end card, -13 or -14, at lend) and into cells 85 on here, with an edge (28) after them. Then
; for each letter (apostrophes skipped) it asks filter for the letter's rules (OUT at req) and tells the context
; machines where the letter is: the left one the cell before it and -1 (OUT at pl1, pl2), the right one the letter's
; cell and 1 (OUT at pr1, pr2), as CLA words. rule.cq answers each rule with the rule's length if it matched, else 0
; (INP at ga), and the next letter is that many on. At the edge, -1 to both context machines (OUT at el, er) and the
; end card on to filter.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            word    CLA   wst      03-26: a card: pass it on, or a word's letter, or its end
  04                    STO   sw
  05            gw      INP   x
  06                    CLA   x
  07                    TAC   neg
  08                    SUB   c28
  09                    TAC   let
  10            pass    OUT   x
  11                    JMP   gw
  12            neg     ADD   c13
  13                    TAC   lo
  14                    SUB   00
  15                    TAC   endw
  16                    JMP   pass
  17            lo      ADD   00
  18                    TAC   pass
  19                    JMP   endw
  20            let     OUT   x
  21                    CLA   x
  22            sw      DATA  0        (STO 85 + n)
  23                    CLA   sw
  24                    ADD   00
  25                    STO   sw
  26                    JMP   gw
  27            endw    CLA   x        27-35: the end: the edge after the word; start at the first letter
  28                    STO   e
  29            lend    OUT   e
  30                    CLA   sw
  31                    STO   se
  32                    CLA   c28
  33            se      DATA  0        (STO the edge)
  34                    CLA   wi
  35                    STO   pi
  36            step    CLA   pi       36-51: the letter: an apostrophe, the edge, or ask for its rules
  37                    STO   rd
  38            rd      DATA  0        (CLA the letter)
  39                    STO   v
  40                    SUB   c27
  41                    TAC   req
  42                    SUB   00
  43                    TAC   apos
  44            el      OUT   m1
  45            er      OUT   m1
  46                    OUT   e
  47                    JMP   word
  48            apos    CLA   pi
  49                    ADD   00
  50                    STO   pi
  51                    JMP   step
  52            req     OUT   v        52-67: ask, tell where, then on by each rule's answer
  53                    CLA   pi
  54                    SUB   00
  55                    STO   t
  56            pl1     OUT   t
  57            pl2     OUT   m1
  58            pr1     OUT   pi
  59            pr2     OUT   00
  60            ga      INP   a
  61                    CLA   a
  62                    SUB   00
  63                    TAC   ga
  64                    CLA   pi
  65                    ADD   a
  66                    STO   pi
  67                    JMP   step
  70            x       DATA  0
  71            e       DATA  0
  72            pi      DATA  0
  73            v       DATA  0
  74            t       DATA  0
  75            a       DATA  0
  76            m1      DATA  -1
  77            c13     DATA  13
  78            c27     DATA  27
  79            c28     DATA  28
  80            wst     STO   85
  81            wi      CLA   85
